<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:lang="en-US" xml:id="ch-module-reflections" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Reflection</title>

  <section>
    <title>Instructions</title>

    <p> The last part of this project is writing a small reflection (1 - 2 pages) about your experiences. We do not expect this document to be highly polished, we want to hear your perspectives and value hearing your individual voice! </p>
    <p>There is no specific format or content you must include, however, below are a few ideas to get you started:</p>
    <p>    
    <ul>
        <li><p>What was your favorite part of this honors experience? Why? What was your least favorite?</p></li>
        <li><p>What was something you learned that surprised you the most?</p></li>
        <li><p>How has this honors project changed the way you think about the Holocaust? What bout the way you think about science and ethics? </p></li>
        <li><p>Will this change in perspective have a lasting effect on you? In what way?</p></li>    
        <li><p> Based on what you've learned, what do you think the general public should know about the Holocaust, STEM, and ethics? </p></li>
        <li><p> How do you plan to practice ethical STEM now and in the future? Is your answer now different from what it would have been at the beginning of the semester?</p></li>
        <li><p> What would you change about this experience? What would you keep the same?</p></li>
    </ul>
    </p>
  </section>
</chapter>
